Honey-colored crystal crowns a broad natural crossing where three
veins of the grotto divide. A crimson shelf climbs north through
iron-red quartz, a cobalt hollow slopes south into colder stone, and a
pale channel leads east where nearly every hue seems to fade. Warm
light pulses gently beneath the floor.
